Noto Sans Syriac Eastern is an unmodulated (sans serif) Madnhaya design
for texts in the Middle Eastern Syriac script. It is the design used
for East Syriac and for Assyrian Neo-Aramaic, also called Swadayya.
It also covers Arabic and Latin characters.

This package installs the complete upstream font set, not the reduced
Google Fonts subset, under /usr/share/fonts/TTF:

  NotoSansSyriacEastern-Thin.ttf, NotoSansSyriacEastern-Regular.ttf,
  NotoSansSyriacEastern-Black.ttf, and the variable font
  NotoSansSyriacEastern[wght].ttf.

The static fonts cover the Thin, Regular, and Black weights. The
variable font adds the ExtraLight, Light, Medium, SemiBold, Bold, and
ExtraBold weights through a weight axis running from 100 to 900.

The fonts are licensed under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1. The
license text is in /usr/doc/ttf-noto-sans-syriac-eastern-<version>/.
